Package: goblin-mode-pro
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.11),
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5),
         python3-psutil,
         policykit-1 | polkitd
Recommends: mangohud, gamemode, gamescope, wl-clipboard, python3-pystray, python3-cairo
Suggests: gpu-screen-recorder
Description: One-switch performance helper for Linux gaming
 Detects a game launching, tunes the CPU governor, process priority,
 compositor and power limits, and reverts them cleanly on exit - then
 watches thermals, frame rate and the Proton log and turns a problem into
 a plain-language report.
 .
 An unprivileged systemd --user daemon does the work; a small polkit-gated
 root helper performs the handful of privileged sysfs writes.

Package: goblin-mode-pro-helper-rust
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, goblin-mode-pro (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Goblin Mode Pro privileged helper, Rust implementation
 The privileged helper rewritten in Rust, serving the same frozen D-Bus
 interface as the Python one. It is the only compiled component, which is why
 it is packaged separately: the main package stays Architecture: all and
 installable everywhere, including on machines this binary is not built for.
 .
 Installing this does NOT switch to it. The unit runs
 /usr/libexec/goblin-mode-pro/helper, a symlink that still points at the
 Python helper. To switch:
 .
   sudo ln -sfn /usr/libexec/goblin-mode-pro/helper-rust \
                /usr/libexec/goblin-mode-pro/helper
   sudo systemctl restart goblin-mode-pro-helper
 .
 Roll back by pointing the symlink at
 /usr/lib/goblin-mode-pro/goblin_helper.py and restarting. The Python helper
 ships in the main package and is always present, so a rollback never needs a
 toolchain.
